# Copy to `.env` and fill in, then restart the dev server.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: getCache_OfflineMap ships with no tile-server origin baked
# in, so that installing it cannot bill someone else's Cloudflare account. The
# child reads VITE_TILES_HOST at boot and configures itself from it.
#
# ⛔ IF IT IS UNSET, THE OFFLINE MAP DOWNLOADS NOTHING AND SAYS ALMOST NOTHING.
# No /pack request is sent at all — packUrl() returns null and the download is
# skipped before the network. The satellite still appears (different service),
# so it looks like "roads are broken" rather than "no tile host configured".
# The only clue is one console.info line at startup.
#
# Point it at your own offline-tiles Worker. Ours is tiles-prod.retreever.org; a
# contractor working on the sandbox should use tiles-dev.retreever.org.
VITE_TILES_HOST=
